 const optics=DATA.phys10Chapters.find(c=>c.num===12), electro=DATA.phys10Chapters.find(c=>c.num===13); if(!optics||!electro||electro.__sourcePdf3Pages1to4)return; electro.__sourcePdf3Pages1to4=true;
 const lens=optics.topics.find(t=>t.num==='12.2');
 if(lens){lens.sourceReferences=lens.sourceReferences||[];lens.sourceReferences.push({pdf:'10thphysics3.pdf',pdfPage:29,printedPage:'103'});lens.sourcePages=lens.sourcePages||[];lens.sourcePages.push({pdf:'10thphysics3.pdf',pdfPage:29,printedPage:'103',paras:[{text:'NUMERICAL QUESTIONS continued: 4. A light ray strikes an air/water surface at 46° to the normal. Water has refractive index 1.33. Find the refraction angle for travel (a) air to water and (b) water to air. 5. An optical fibre core of flint glass (n=1.66) is surrounded by crown-glass cladding (n=1.52). Find the critical angle. 6. A book page 7.50 cm from a convex lens of focal length 10.0 cm and a concave lens of focal length −10 cm: find magnification in each case. 7. Gulalai views a flea with a magnifier f=3.0 cm and near point N=25 cm; find maximum magnification. 8. A telescope has magnification 40.0 and length 1230 mm; find objective and eyepiece focal lengths.'}]});}
